<ansi fg="header">Help for retreat</ansi>

retreat [exit] — withdraw your present company from its battle.
retreat — choose the first legal visible exit in alphabetical order.

One combat round prepares the withdrawal. The next attempts escape.
Repeating the order keeps its countdown. A failed attempt resumes fighting.
Your leader gives up those attacks. One available guardian can spend a guard
and its preparation attack to cover the company: +15 percentage points.
A chanting guardian cannot cover. Cover is lost if that guardian falls or
leaves before the attempt. Existing guards still intercept incoming blows.

The slowest present living member sets the company's mobility. Speed is
reduced by personal burden (up to 60%) and lasting wounds (up to 30%).
Against the fastest active pursuer, the chance is:
30 + 70 × company mobility / (company mobility + pursuer mobility), plus cover.
It stays between 30% and 95%; without pursuers the company escapes for sure.
Waiting groups do not block your withdrawal.

A living member unable to move holds the company here. No-go/no-flee hurts,
locks, missing exits and room permissions are rechecked each round.
A member transferred or moved elsewhere cancels the order. Fallen companions
stay subject to resurrection; retreat cannot revive them. Members who already
lost nerve keep their saved return obligation, including the 5-loyalty debt.
New arrivals, other companies, pets and temporary charms are not swept along.

Successful withdrawal moves the same live members, ends your battle and clears
its targets, casts and guards. Interrupted casts receive no retreat refund.
Other players' battles continue. Company cargo and the herd remain the same
owned records and follow their normal location rules; nothing is copied.
A restart or copyover cancels the runtime order; it cannot move a saved company.

flee remains emergency personal escape. Blocked living companions separate
using the existing saved return system and rejoin when the battle ends, for
5 loyalty. If that separation cannot be saved, you remain in the battle;
already saved flights still rejoin once, when it ends. See help flee,
help morale, help guardian, help burden and help company.
